hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-lines-9 : List (List Word)
hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-lines-9 = cons "*Type* is Greek *typos*, the mark left by a blow, from *typtein*, to strike. A type is an impression: what a stamp leaves in wax. A value of a type is something that bears that impression. *Character*, Greek *kharaktēr*, is the engraving tool and the mark it makes. So a typed language is a language of stamps and impressions, and the checker reads the impression to know what struck it." (cons "" nil)
